            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I'm tracing the pattern: the 6-marker seems to indicate a wall position, and depending on whether it's on the left column, bottom row, or right column, a diagonal line gets drawn from a specific corner along with a 4-line on the opposite edge\u2014so the transformation rule involves mapping wall position to diagonal direction plus an edge fill.\n\nI notice the pattern: the 6 line rotates counterclockwise to determine where the 4 line goes\u2014left becomes bottom, bottom becomes right, right becomes top\u2014and in each case the 4 line occupies that perpendicular edge except for the single cell it shares with the 6 line's corner.\n\nThe diagonal cells then run from the corner opposite the meeting point, tracing the anti-diagonal while excluding that shared corner cell itself, which checks out consistently across all three cases.",
